with no statement, the exported variable is what the probe key resolves to: true
a raw write to the config-file table is outranked by the exported variable: true
a stated key outranks the exported variable, and says it was stated in process: true
Utils.stated_config reads the statement back: true
withdrawing the statement leaves the exported variable answering again: true
unstated, the profile key resolves to the commandline-picked profile's payload: true
a stated key outranks a commandline-picked profile and an exported variable alike: true
inside with_stated_config, its statements are read: true
after a raising body, the prior statement and the prior absence are back: true
a stated key's record renders as an in-process source, layer and origin: true
a statement agreeing with the commandline is accepted: true
a statement contradicting the commandline is refused, naming the key and the argument: true
a contradicted statement leaves no statement behind: true
a statement of a key in a spelling no read looks up, or one no read registers, is refused, naming the key: true
a statement of a key resolved at initialization is refused, naming the key: true
a statement of a settings snapshot is refused, naming the key: true
a startup-only input or compatibility spelling is refused, naming the key: true
